WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.860
Take two everyday verbs: «aller»,

2
00:00:02.860 --> 00:00:06.250
to go, and «manger», to eat.

3
00:00:06.250 --> 00:00:07.480
Put them in the past,

4
00:00:07.480 --> 00:00:09.500
and make the subject a girl.

5
00:00:09.500 --> 00:00:12.480
'She ate' is spelt just as you'd expect.

6
00:00:12.480 --> 00:00:16.090
But 'she went' picks up an
extra letter on the end.

7
00:00:16.090 --> 00:00:18.400
Same girl. Same tense.

8
00:00:18.400 --> 00:00:21.090
So why does 'she went'
get an extra letter,

9
00:00:21.090 --> 00:00:23.360
when 'she ate' never does?

10
00:00:23.360 --> 00:00:26.500
In this mission, you'll
explore a house full of verbs,

11
00:00:26.500 --> 00:00:28.820
from the front gate to the stairs.

12
00:00:28.820 --> 00:00:30.910
Then you'll flip switches in the lab,

13
00:00:30.910 --> 00:00:34.090
predict first, and see which verbs react.

14
00:00:34.090 --> 00:00:38.430
Your mission: work out which verbs
add the extra letter, and when.
